# SABOTAGE: issue #72 — the summarize call stops opting into `error_usage`, so the
# chokepoint narrows a usage-carrying failure to `{:error, reason}`. A summarizer that
# overflows mid-generation (Anthropic's `model_context_window_exceeded`, a real, billed
# call) is then billed nothing, exactly the gap #72 was split out of #11 to close.
#
# Flips the failed-summarizer billing test. Successful and ingress-refused summaries still
# bill (they are `{:ok, _}` completions), so only a usage-carrying FAILURE catches it.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_durability_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: #72 RED: a summarize call that FAILS reporting usage is billed (a summarizer that overflows)
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/compaction.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/compaction.ex
index bd11e848..87acdd70 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/compaction.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/compaction.ex
@@ -106,7 +106,8 @@ defmodule Samen.AI.Agent.Compaction do
       [Samen.AI.Agent.summarizer_prompt()],
       %{},
       [
-        {:error_usage, true}
+        # SABOTAGE (#72): the summarize call does not ask the chokepoint for a failure's usage.
+        {:error_usage, false}
         | Samen.AI.Agent.egress_opts(opts, folded, [], structure(folded, model))
       ]
     )
